body:
These were our Painted Pictographic Histories that are spoken of as Ilbʼal re Popo Wuj; those Painted Pounded Paper Lienzo-Ilbʼal Poj-Poj-Wuj no longer exist so they no longer can be contemplated to be known; for they no longer can be seen to be ponder.

And so it is we shall write out our Ancestral Account here to tell of our lives lived in the shadows-qamujibʼal before the Saqil Kʼolem; Saqil Tzij the Perfection of Existence; Perfection of the Word of God-uchʼabʼal Dios; the Perfect Life of Christianity-pa Christianoil-the Precious Life as it is said: Ilbʼal Saq Kʼaslem-the Painted Pictures of the Sacred Life; the Divine Life. We tell of all that happen before in the Perfection of Being; in the Perfection of the Word: Saqil Kʼolem; Saqil Tzij.

There exist the First Books-Nabʼey Wujil with their Ancient Script-Ojer Tzibʼam but those who can read their inscriptions to contemplate their meaning only hide their face for they no longer want to be seen to be known as the Seers-Ilol and Contemplators-Bʼisol who are the Knowers-Naʼol of the Ancient Books with their Ancestral Writing.

Yet once great was the Long Performance of the Recitation; of the Incantation that brought forth the complete emergence of the Sky-Earth; Kaj-Ulew. Spoken of as:

Its Four-fold Cornering of the Corners; its Four-Fold Siding of the Sides;

Its Four-fold Cornering; its Four-fold Siding;

Its being stretched-out; its being measured-out;

Its Four-fold staking of the Four-fold Corners;

Its Four-fold staking of the Four-fold Sides;

Its being measured by halving the measuring cord in two;

Its being measured by doubling its measuring cord in half;

Its stretching of its measuring cord to meet the Center of the Sky;

Its stretching of its measuring cord to meet the Center of the Earth;

Its stretching of its umbilical cord up into the Womb of the Sky;

Its stretching of its umbilical cord down into the Womb of the Earth;

The Four Corners; the Four Sides as it is said by those known as the Former, as the Shaper; named Tzʼaqol, Bʼitol.

Ukaj Tzʼuq, Ukaj Xukutaxik; retaxik;

Ukaj Cheʼxik, Umej Kʼaʼmaxik Upa Kaj, Upa Ulew;

Kaj Tzʼuq, Kaj Xukut, chuchaʼxik rumal Tzʼaqol, Bʼitol;

Chimalmat as Shield-Bearer is a warrior-woman who defends her people by wielding the shield-chimalli that she bears in her hand. But this chimalli that is a shield is transformed into a weapon by fixing obsidian blades all around its outer edge.

This then was when Sipakna played about-Chaaj on the Face of the Earth by ʼmaking ash-chajʼ with his constant eruptions; it is said that he just ʼplayed-chaajʼ with the Great Mountains-Nimaq Juyubʼ that were the Great Volcanoes known and named as:

Chi Qʼaqʼ: Mouth of Fire Volcano, Volcán de Fuego;

Jun Ajpu: One Blow-gun Boy, Volcán de Agua;

IxPekul Ya: Water Cave of the Landslide Volcano, Volcán de Santo Tomás;

Yaxkanul:  New Volcano, Volcán de Santa María;

Makamob: Gathered Stone of Molten Lava, Cerro Quemado;

Julisnab: Tendril-Hair Root of the Cave of Flower Mountain, Volcán Almolonga.

Just one night was all that was needed for Sipakna to complete his work;  just one night was all it took for him to create a mountain. Just one night was time enough for Sipakna to bring forth a Great Mountain-Nima Juyubʼ spoken of today as a Volcano.

Ordering of Nature by the Cultural Heroes

These are the names given to the Great Mountain-Volcanoes that rose-up to stand there before the Dawn of the Maize People at the Dawn of the Kʼicheʼ Sun. This is an ancient world of mountain making giants that took place during the ancient ancestral Sun of the Wooden People who die in a Flood of Qʼol-Resin created by this Volcano Boy known as the Spiny One, the Smoking One: Sipakna.

Sipakna is often portrayed  standing-up as the Ceiba Tree that is conflated with the ʼspiny backʼ of Sipakna also known as Cipacatli, the Great Crocodile, Great Caiman Earth Monster Deity known as Tlaltecuhtli. This image of the Great Caiman Earth is easily seen from the Pacific Ocean shore from the Pacific shore town of Cipacatli by looking up towards the Highlands.

The Messenger Owls perched themselves above the ballcourt to ʼthrow downʼ their message like a ball thrown-tzaq into play. They did this in order to ʼmake-tzʼaqʼ their words just exactly as they were ʼmade-tzʼaqʼ by the Lords to be repeated precisely, with precision, as perfectly ordered words ʼmadeʼ to be repeated as the perfect repetition of words ʼthrown down into playʼ just as they were sent to be said as the message from the Lords of Xibʼalbʼa-Ajawabʼ Xibʼalbʼa. This was when they, the Lords, sent their message to be repeated to the ball-players who played there on their Ballcourt-Jom known as Nim Xol Kar Chaaj.

And so it was that the Owls sent the message sent by those of Xibʼalbʼa:

Jun Kame, Wuqubʼ Kame;

Ajal Puj, Ajal Qʼana;

Chʼamiya Bʼaq, Chʼamiya Jolom;

Xikiripat, Kuchumakikʼ;

Ajal Mes, Ajal Toqʼobʼ;

Xik, Patan, this was the precise order of the names of the Noble Lords and Rulers of Death and Disease, ri Ajawabʼ Xibʼalbʼa.

Itʼs time you are told: AjAwabʼ means those of ʼillness-yawabʼ-diseaseʼ which a play on the plural of name of Ajaw-Lord which is Ajawabʼ or Lords. So this is an amazing play on the name of the Lords of Xibʼalbʼa who are called Ajawabʼ Xibʼalbʼa who are Lords of Disease Ajawabʼ Yawabʼ which is really quite a play on names that are words and this is why I refuse to translate Ajawabʼ if possible because this is how the Scribes of Ancient Word of this Ancestral Account ʼnamed the namesʼ of the Lords of Xibʼalbʼa:  Ajawabʼ Xibʼalbʼa.

And so the message of the Lords-Ajawabʼ was formed-xtzʼaq by the messengers; the message that was thrown down-xtzaq by their messengers, the Owls-Tukur, so that their words were received as a challenge thrown into play by the Owls who formed their words just right so they were received as the words of the Lords that were formed by the Owls to then be thrown down into play by the Owls there in the ballcourt by the Owls-xtzaq kitzij kumal Tukur, as it is said. This challenge that the Owls made on behalf of the Lords was thrown down on the ballcourt to the ballplayers who listened in disbelief to all the Messengers said.

These limestone stelae were carved and sculpted there to invoke the Kabʼawil to whom the tree-stones were dedicated with engraved inscriptions; sculpted images and carved figures of the First Mother-Fathers; Nabʼe Chuch-Qajaw who were those known as the Ancient Ones; Nawal Winaq; Ancestral People.

They just thought about the Sowing when they remembered the Dawning; for truly this then was when they anxiously anticipated the Dawn as a soulful remembrance of what was to come as a heartfelt reminiscence of the Sowing; a recollection of the Dawning that awaited them there at the Coming Out Place of the Sun: Relebʼal Qʼij.

Xere kikʼuxlaʼn ri rewaxik; usaqirik;

There heart-felt remembrance of the Sowing; the Dawning

Truly excited were they to be so very animated because of their soulful remembrance and recollection of their duty and dedication to bring forth the Sowing of the New Era; the Dawning of the New Sun; the Creation of the New Age which was their sacred obligation-patan; which was their divine burden-patan to be borne-patan on their back to carry in the tumpline-patan slung across and over the crown of their head-kijolom-their skull; the carrying of the ancestral cargo-patan that was theirs to carry: the Sowing; the Dawning: Rewaxik; Saqarik. This was their divine burden to be borne out on their back. This is what they now remembered as they anxiously awaited the Sowing; of the Dawning. Xere kikʼuxlaʼn ri rewaxik; usaqirik.

It was to the Sowing just as it was to the Dawning that they made their humble request; just praying with great reverence did they make their affection appeal before the Dawn; for they were those who made their needs known through their sweet plea; through their powerful petition to the Kabʼawil who were gathered there before the Sowing, the Dawning-Rewaxik Saqarik.

They were those of beloved words; of the precious truth-e loqʼ tzij;

These were the loving ones; the kind ones; the sweet ones-e ajloqʼ;

It was they who were the beloved people; the adored people-e ajloqʼ;

They who were the meek ones; the modest ones-e ajnim-humble ones;

They the obedient ones; the dutiful, devoted, dedicated one-e ajnim;

These were the reverent ones; respectful ones-e ajxobʼ;

These were those of deep respect; people of high regard-e ajxobʼ;

For it was they who gave sacrifice to sustain and maintain the Sky-Earth; Kaj-Ulew for this indeed was who they were and who their descendants would come to be.

They raised their faces to the Heavens-chikipaqʼabaʼ kiwach chi Kaj;

They lifted their eyes to the Sky-chikipaqʼabaʼ kiwach chi Kaj;

Praying for their Daughters; Pleading for their Sons;

Imploring, insisting upon the Sky; they just imposed as they impressed upon the Heart of the Sky; Heart of the Earth-Ukʼuʼx Kaj; Ukʼuʼx Ulew their needs.

With their Eyes raised to the Sky; With their Eyes raised to the Heavens

With their hearts set afire and their soul filled with desire they brought forth their words that burned ablaze as if on a sacrificial pyre calling out for all that they aspired and wished to acquire for their entire lot of their descendant daughters and resplendent sons.

This then was when they began to beg and beseech; implore and entreat Ukʼuʼx Kaj; Ukʼuʼx Ulew with secret sacred speech for all that they needed making a plea as they pleaded for their wants and wishes  to be conceded on behalf of their Pueblo and People for whom they would most willingly bleed.

This then was when they began their prayer; their petition for all that was required; for all that was requested and desired for their beloved Sons and Daughters on the Face of the Earth.

Thus they intone with true inspiration their incantation, invocation, and enchantment of their honored, admired, and revered Kabʼawil:

“Aqaroq; Saqaroq; To the Rising Sun, To the Coming of the Dawn!

At Tzʼaqol, At Bʼitol!

You Former, You Shaper;

You Molder, You Modeler;

You Crafter, You Creator;

You Plotter, You Planner!

You Builder, You Maker!

AjTzʼaq, AjBʼit!

Look upon us! Kojawilaʼ!

Listen to us! Kojata!

Do not forget us! Mojatzaqo! Donʼt abandon us!

Do not discard us! Mojapiskʼalij! Do not leave us!

Oh You Divine Deity in the Sky;

Oh Deified Divinity upon the Earth!

At Kabʼawil chi Kaj, chi Ulew!

Heart of the Sky, Heart of the Earth; Ukʼux Kaj, Ukʼux Ulew

These Primordial Mountains are where the Principal Lineage of the Kʼicheʼ live out their primordial ancestral lives on the Original Mountain Places they found as those known as Our First Four Mother-Fathers; QaNabʼe Chuch-Qajaw of the Kʼicheʼ Maya Kingdom with its Primordial Lineages and their Primordial Mountain Places: Chi Pixabʼ; Jaqawitz; Chui Juyubʼ; Chi Ismachi; Qʼumaraq Aaj; Santa Cruz del Quicheʼ…

And on and on it will go with the changing and transforming of the Mountain Places; Pa Juyubʼal of the ʼMountain Tribesʼ and the Noble Lords of the Great House coming to live on these Primordial Mountains of the Original Primordial Mountain People who lived on these ʼLivable Mountainsʼ before the arrival of the Kʼicheʼ Warlords and Captains who carry-out their Conquest and Settlement of the Mountain People and their Mountain Places.

All of which comes to its inevitable end with the arrival of the Castilian Captains and Warlords guided and protected by a New Sun known as Tonatiuh or Donadiu the Castilian Conquistador el Adelantado Don Pedro de Alvarado who like the Great Star Venus bears the New Age of the New Sun of the New Lords of the Land known as Kaxlan Winaq; Castilian People.

Letʼs go, letʼs get going! We must find these Kabʼawil we seek in our quest to find the One who will guide and protect us by speaking to us on our way back to our Mountains from our place here in Tollan Tzuy-Wa. Let us then find to One who will accompany us to the Forest Realm of the Many Trees of Our Highland Forest of We, the First Four Noble Lords of the Kʼicheʼ.

They heard word of Citadel and this is where they went. The name of that Citadel; Tinamit was Juyubʼ Waʼ which was known as Mountain of Sustenance that was indeed spoken of as Sustenance Mountain and this is where they went; those known and named:

Bʼalam Kiʼtzeʼ;

Bʼalam Aqʼabʼ;

Majukʼutaj;

Ikʼi Bʼalam

This is the name of the Citadel-Tinamit-Ciudadela they went to, in order to arrive at the splendid city sown and seated at the very center of the great empire of Quetzalcoatl: Tulan.

It was then that the Tribes arrived again before the Kabʼawil. They were just being finished off by the bitter cold drafts of freezing cold air that dropped from the icy sky, thick with hail-saqboch, as the earth became drenched with dense black rain-qʼeqʼal jabʼ that turned to ice as it froze covering the ground with white frost: saqʼbʼoqom.

Intolerable was the unbearable icy cold that they bundled themselves up against; the Tribes; Amaqʼ, one and all, could no longer tolerate the freezing cold that left them crawling about on all fours like animals to arrive there before those were the First Four Fathers:

Bʼalam Kiʼtzeʼ;

Bʼalam Aqʼabʼ;

Majukʼutaj;

Ikʼi Bʼalam

Immense was the affliction of these cursed souls because of the insufferable cold. They covered their mouths; they covered their faces as they came to plead their desperate situation before the Noble Lords who they begged and beseeched to show them mercy by doing them a favor; those who were:

Bʼalam Kiʼtzeʼ;

Bʼalam Aqʼabʼ;

Majukʼutaj;

Ikʼi Bʼalam

“Will you not show us mercy so that we might ask you a favor? Could it be that maybe you might perhaps find it in your hearts to give us a bit of your fire; a small bundle of flames that you might give us; we the Tribes; we the Pueblos; ri Amaqʼ?” and so they continued to speak as they made their case as best they could.

“Havenʼt you gathered it up already? Have you not already found it? For it was just One Ancestral Place of Origin that we called Home; it was just One Ancestral Mountain that we shared together; just One Mountain Place of Origin from which we came forth as One; for it was just One Ancestral Home of Origin that we came to know as our own from when you were formed; from when you were shaped; are we not One?  Please then, do us this one favor!” pleaded the People of the Pueblos.

“What is it that you should give us so that we might show you our kindness; that we might do you this one favor?” asked Bʼalam Kiʼtzeʼ, Bʼalam Aqʼabʼ.

“Utz! Fine! Good! Utz!  We will give you precious metal; silver is what we will give you,” said then the Tribes.

“May this which I leave with you serve as a remembrance of me; may this that I leave with you enable you to form-prayers, to shape-petitions; to make-prayers, to perform-petitions to me and before me your Grandfather, Father-Mam, Qajaw. This is your power-qʼaqʼal-this is your strength; this your fire; this your ember; this is your spark; this is your flame to ignite the light of your radiance,” he said when he left his sign-retal-of remembrance, his transformative essence-ukʼojeʼik-his divine nature of his Nawal Soul: Pisom Qʼaqʼal-Sacred Bundle of Burning Embers; Sacred Bundle of Ancestral Power; Ancestral Fire for the  Incantation and Invocation of Divine Remembrance; Prayer and Petition of Ancestral Power:

Sacred Bundle of Ancestral Fire

Sacred Bundle of Ancestral Soul;

Sacred Bundle of Ancestral Seed;

Sacred Bundle of Ancestral Star;

Sacred Bundle of Ancestral Spirit;

Sacred Bundle of Ancestral Essence of Nawal Perfection;

Sacred Bundle of Ancestral Essence of Ancestral Power:

Pisom Qʼaqʼal Bʼalam Kiʼtzeʼ.”

This is the ʼfire-qʼaqʼal-powerʼ Bʼalam Kiʼtzeʼ earned through his fasting while walking is ritual pilgrimage as ritual sacrifice. This was the ʼfire, ember-qʼaqʼal-strength, powerʼ Bʼalam Kiʼtzeʼ was gifted when it was bestowed upon him as a sacred burden to bear on his back, shoulders, and crown of his head when he bore up the tumpline-patan-pack strap of the sacred burden given to him to be taken up by his there at Tulan Tzuy-Wa. The sacred burden of his Kabʼawil Tojil was now passed on through the Sacred Bundle: Pisom Qʼaqʼal

Its face could not be seen being wrapped up in a Sacred Bundle as it was, so hidden, so covered, so very bundled-up, so sown shut. But it was there that presence Bʼalam Kiʼtzeʼ and Tojil were felt as the heart; were sensed as the soul of the ancestral remembrance that burns as the ʼfire-qʼaqʼal-emberʼ in this Sacred Bundle: Pisom Qʼaqʼal.

Sacred Bundle: Pisom Qʼaqʼal

This then is the petitioning before the divine countenance of the Kʼicheʼ Kabʼawil; the calling out, the crying out to beg, to beseech; to request, to require; to implore, to entreat; to plead, to pray, to petition; to solicit, to supplicate; to ask for in order to make oneʼs final appeal heard by the Lord of the Five Days  known to us here as Quetzalcoatl; the Great Star known s the Morning Star; the Evening Star in his Fiver Forms and Phases known by Four Names of the Five Days of the Year-Bearers; known as the Mam; the Ancient Old Ancestor; Grandfather who takes the form of the transforming image of the changing and transforming Maize Deity with all the many forms that take the many shapes of Sacred Sustenance.

These Five Divine Days also refer to the Five Days of the Year-Bearer and perhaps it was on these Five Days that the Five Sections of the Popol Wuj were played out; one Story of Origins played out on each Night of each of the Days; played out like Twins to reveal the Twinship of the Sun and Venus; Moon and the Sun; Venus and the Moon. This then is the prayer of invocation of the Story of Forming; the Story of Shaping told on each Night of these Days known as the Wayebʼ. The Wayebʼ embody this Five Day period of the changing and transforming ʼNawal Wayʼ of these Five Divine Days.

You of the Sacred Five Days

Aqʼaroq! You of the Sacred Five Days; At Oobʼ uqʼij;

You the One-Footed-One; Juraqan; Jun Raqan

You, Heart of the Sky, At Ukʼuʼx Kaj;

You, Heart of the Earth, At Ukʼuʼx Ulew;

You, Giver of Abundance, Giver of Sustenance; At yaʼol rech Qʼanal; Raxal

You, Shimmering Shining One; Qʼanal

You, Radiant Resplendent One; Raxal

And you Giver of Daughters, you Giver of Sons; At pu yaʼol Miʼal, Kʼajol!

May there be a Scattering of Jade; May there Fall a Rain of Splendor

Chatziloj, Chamaqʼij uloq a Raxal; a Qʼanal

May your Blessings be Sown Out; May your Gifts be Given Out;

May your Radiance Rain Down with Sacred Sustenance;

May there be a Great Scattering of Jade Resplendence;

May there be a Shining Shimmering Sparkling Abundance;

Chayaʼ taj Kʼaseʼik, Winaqirik Wal, Nukʼajol!

Give Life and Formation to Our Children; Our Sprouts

Place them on Resplendent Roads of Shinny Riches; of Golden Abundance;

Keʼayaʼ tak pa Raxa Bʼe, pa Raxa Jok!

Place them on a Radiant Road; Place them on a Wide Open Walkways;

Keʼayaʼ tak pa Raxa Bʼe, pa Raxa Jok!

May they not find evil doing; Ma ta ja bʼi kil

Ma ta ja bʼi kil; kitzʼap; akʼwil; awitzmal;

May there be no wrong doing; traps; ambush; shame; disgrace;

May there be no misfortune; snares, witchcraft; evil conjuring

May they not find any trap or ambush on their way; Ma ta ja bʼi kitzʼap;

May they meet with no disgrace; Ma ta ja bʼi akʼwil;

May they meet with no misfortune; Ma ta ja bʼi akʼwil;

May they not find witchcraft; Ma ta ja bʼi awitzmal;

May they suffer no evil conjuring; Ma ta ja bʼi awitzmal;

May those who provide for you be of excellent ways; refined nature;

May those who sustain you be of a fine essence; a fine character;

May those who provide be of excellent words and ways;

May those who sustain you be of fine in speech, beautiful traits;

You Heart of the Sky, You Heart of the Earth;

At Ukʼuʼx Kaj; At Ukʼuʼx Ulew

You, Sacred Bundle of Fire, of Flames; Pisom Qʼaqʼal

Sacred Bundle of Power: Pisom Qʼaqʼal

You, Sacred Bundle; Pisom Qʼaqʼal;

Sacred Bundle of the Ancestral Spirit; Pisom Qʼaqʼal

Burning Bundle of the Ancestral Soul; Pisom Qʼaqʼal

You, who are known as Tojil, Awilix, Jaqawitz;

Womb of the Sky, Upam Kaj;

Womb of the Earth, Upam Ulew;

Kaj Tzʼuq, Kaj Xukut; Four-fold Cornering, Four-fold Siding

You of the Four Corners; Kaj Tzʼuq

You of the Four Sides; Kaj Xukut

May there be Peace, Xa ta Saq;

May their be Divinity, Xa ta Saq;

May there be Perfection, Xa ta Saq;

May there be Clarity, Xa ta Saq;

May there be Tranquility in Community, Xa ta Amaqʼ

May there by Peace, Xa ta Saq;

May their be Harmony, Xa ta Amaqʼ

You Resplendent Divinity of the Sacred People of the Harmonious Pueblo,

May Radiant Peace shine in beside and before your Eternal Name: Kabʼawil

Xa ta Saq; Xa ta Amaqʼ upam chachi, chawach; at Kabʼawil

Aqʼaroq! At oobʼ uqʼij,

at Juraqan, at Ukʼuʼx Kaj-Ulew!

At ya-ol rech qʼanal, raxal,

at pu yaʼol miʼal, kʼajol!”

Chatziloj, chamaqʼij uloq a raxal, a qʼanal!
